  "description": "The Burrowing Owl is a small owl of open country, distinguished by long legs, yellow eyes, and a rounded head without ear tufts. Brown plumage marked with pale spots helps it blend into dry grass and rocky ground. Unlike many owls, it is often active in daylight and may watch its surroundings from a low perch. It catches insects and small animals close to the ground. Burrows provide nesting sites, often in places where ground squirrels or other digging mammals have already created underground shelter.",
